<article class="env-lemma" id="05C0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05C0">Lemma <span data-tag="05C0">10.63.17</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $M$ be an $R$-module. Let $S \subset R$ be a multiplicative subset. Assume that every $s \in S$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Ass}_ R(M) = \text{Ass}_ R(S^{-1}M).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As $M \subset S^{-1}M$ by assumption we get the inclusion $\text{Ass}(M) \subset \text{Ass}(S^{-1}M)$ from Lemma <a href="/tag/02M3" data-tag="02M3">10.63.3</a>. Conversely, suppose that $n/s \in S^{-1}M$ is an element whose annihilator is a prime ideal $\mathfrak p$. Then the annihilator of $n \in M$ is also $\mathfrak p$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>